.TH DIFFVIM-COMPARE 1 "2026-08-18" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim-compare \- benchmark diff algorithms and option combinations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim-compare
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>
.RI [ output_dir ]
.br
.B diffvim-compare
.B \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim-compare
generates a matrix of precomputed diff files using every combination of
diff algorithm and post-processing option, then prints a comparison
table so you can pick the most efficient and most readable combination
for your file pair.

It uses the C++ compute tool
.RI ( compute/bin/diffvim-compute-cpp )
under the hood. For each combination it records hunk count, total ops,
delete/insert counts, and compute time, then writes the diff file to the
output directory for offline inspection.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I oldfile
Old version of the file to compare (required).
.TP
.I newfile
New version of the file to compare (required).
.TP
.I output_dir
Where to write the .diff files (default:
.IR /tmp/diffvim-compare ).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.

.SH ALGORITHMS
Two algorithms are exercised:
Patience,
.BR patience .
See
.BR diffvim (1)
for the semantics of each.
(Myers was removed in the refactor.)

.SH OPTION COMBINATIONS
Eight combinations of post-processing flags are exercised:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
(default — no flags)
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-word-diff
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-semantic-cleanup
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-indent-aware
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-word-diff \-\-semantic-cleanup
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-word-diff \-\-indent-aware
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-semantic-cleanup \-\-indent-aware
.IP \(bu 3
\-\-word-diff \-\-semantic-cleanup \-\-indent-aware
.RE

This produces 2 \(mu 8 = 16 diff files in the output directory, named
.IR <algorithm>-<options>.diff .

.SH OUTPUT
For each combination, a single line is printed to stdout:
.IP
.B
<algorithm> <options>  hunks=<N>  ops=<N>  changed=<N>  (del=<N> ins=<N>)  compute: <ms> ms
.PP
Lower
.I changed
= more efficient (fewer insert/delete ops for the viewer).
Lower
.I ops
= shorter animation.
Fewer
.I hunks
= more coherent changes (less cursor movement).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_COMPUTE_BIN
Override the path to the compute binary (default:
.IR compute/bin/diffvim-compute-cpp ).
Historically this also pointed at the
.IR c ,
.IR rust ,
or
.I go
variants, but those were removed in the refactor.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B diffvim-compare examples/42_large_huge_python/old.py examples/42_large_huge_python/new.py
Compare all algorithm/option combinations on a large Python file pair.
.TP
.B diffvim-compare a.py b.py /tmp/mycompare
Write diff files to
.I /tmp/mycompare
instead of the default.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_COMPUTE_BIN=compute/bin/diffvim-compute-cpp diffvim-compare a.py b.py
Explicitly select the C++ compute tool (the default).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR diffvim-compute (1),
.BR diffvim-jogger (1)
.br
.I docs/OPTION_COMBINATIONS.md
and
.I docs/DIFF_STUDY.md
contain detailed analysis.
